The encoder outputs are quantized using a Gumbel‑Softmax with temperature \tau_k. We use an annealing schedule \tau_k = \tau_0 \exp(-\lambda k) that satisfies the Robbins‑Monro conditions. Under mild regularity on the V‑entropy Lagrangian, the soft assignments converge almost surely to a hard codebook, and the expected distortion and rate converge to those of the optimal discrete quantizer. The OverwritePenalty is now explicitly linked to the Size‑Fidelity Paradox thresholds from Guo et al.: using mutual information rank analysis, we set \tau_I such that I(\hat{\mathbf{H}}; \mathbf{H}) \leq \tau_I where \tau_I is the critical mutual information beyond which knowledge overwriting (factual collision) probability exceeds 5%. \tau_I depends on the semantic capacity of the drafter, measured via the effective rank of its embedding space.

